# DUP - Check, format or copy a disk

```text
DUP
DUP /CHECK drive:
```

## Check a disk

DUP works on whole disks. /CHECK reads the selected disk for unreadable
sectors. Set the correct disk format with [CONFIG](CONFIG.HLP) before
checking.

```text
DUP /CHECK D:
```

## Copy or format

```text
DUP /COPY A: D:
DUP /FORMAT D:
```

/COPY writes the contents of the first disk onto the second disk.
/FORMAT prepares the named disk for use. Both replace data on the
destination. Check the mounted destination before confirming. Use
[COPY](COPY.HLP) for individual files.
